public static int computeUTF8Size(CharSequence str, int index, int len) {
    int charIndex = index;
    int result = 0;

    while (charIndex < index + len) {
        int utf8Length = 1;
        char c = str.charAt(charIndex);

        // Check if the character is a continuation byte
        if ((c & 0x80) == 0x80) {
            utf8Length = 2;
            if ((c & 0xC0) == 0xC0) {
                utf8Length = 3;
                if ((c & 0xE0) == 0xE0) {
                    utf8Length = 4;
                }
            }
        }

        charIndex += utf8Length;
        result += utf8Length;
    }

    return result;
}
```
The `computeUTF8Size` method returns the number of bytes in the UTF-8 encoding of a specified substring of the given `CharSequence`. It iterates through each character in the substring, calculating the number of bytes needed to represent the character. If the character is within the ASCII range, it takes up 1 byte. If the character is a multi-byte Unicode character (more than one byte), it takes up multiple bytes based on its UTF-8 encoding. The method keeps a running total of the number of bytes and returns the final result.

